        "headline": "Ella Freire",
        "quote": "I have always had a bit of an obsession with all things tickets and luggage labels.",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Ella_ABOUT_2_1aed916c-93be-467f-bbe3-317c24313873.jpg",
        "body": "<p>Ella Freire is a London-based screen printing artist who has worked from Delta House Studios in Wimbledon for the past 14 years. After a career in interior design she returned to her first love, screen printing, drawn back by the tactile, hands-on nature of the process.</p><p>Her work grows from a long-held fascination with the ephemera of travel: tickets, stamps, and above all the destination luggage tags of the 1960s and 70s. Each print is hand-pulled at gallery scale, colour by colour, recreating the originals down to their perforated edges and punched holes.</p><p>The result is a body of work that captures the romance of the Golden Age of Travel, reimagined as collectible limited-edition art.</p>",
